## Promotion criteria (fixed 2026-10-26, before any rerun)

A variant becomes the S1 candidate only if, in-sample 2016-01-01..2021-12-31:
- MAR ≥ 0.6, longest drawdown < 500 sessions, ≥ 100 trades;
- CAGR above NIFTY 500 TRI over the same window;
- CAGR with the 5 best trades removed ≥ half the CAGR (not carried by outliers);
- no entry above 5% of 20-day average traded value;
- `binding.no_op` false against its base, and each key parameter one step either side keeps MAR ≥ 0.5
  (plateau, not a tuned peak).
Hold-out 2022-01-01..2026-10-23, run once for the candidate: expectancy ≥ half the in-sample
expectancy and MAR ≥ 0.4. After that, paper trading is the only out-of-sample test.
No run cap (owner 2026-10-27): every variant still counts in `dsr_n_trials`, so more runs make the DSR bar stricter.

The same criteria, machine-readable (2026-10-26): `python -m app.hat.backtest.review <run_id>
--criteria <this file> [--sweep <plateau sweep>]` computes each row from the run folders and pins
this block's sha256 in the run's `criteria.md`. The plateau's key parameters and steps were not
written above; the block names the paths the `np` set changes (time stop, SMA exit, swing-low
lookback, partial, VCP minimum contractions) with the steps shown (owner to confirm before the
plateau sweep). The budget counts this round's runs; the 56 variants of the deleted sweeps 1–10
are seeded as prior trials, so they count in `dsr_n_trials` but not against the 30.

```hat-criteria
strategy: S1
universe: NIFTY500_PIT
in_sample: {from: 2016-01-01, to: 2021-12-31}
hold_out: {from: 2022-01-01, to: 2026-10-23}
trial_budget: 10000
checks:
  mar_min: 0.6
  longest_dd_sessions_below: 500
  trades_min: 100
  cagr_above_benchmark: true
  cagr_ex_top5_min_share: 0.5
  max_pct_adv: 5
  binding_required: true
plateau:
  mar_min: 0.5
  parameters:
    - {path: strategy.exits.2.enabled}
    - {path: strategy.exits.3.sma, step: 10}
    - {path: strategy.exits.4.lookback_days, step: 5}
    - {path: strategy.exits.5.enabled}
    - {path: strategy.playbooks.0.setup.criteria.11.params.contractions.0, step: 1}
hold_out_checks:
  expectancy_min_share: 0.5
  mar_min: 0.4
```

## Decisions

- 2026-10-26: results before today deleted (owner: not reliable). Leads to re-check under the new
  standard, not conclusions: wide exits (no time stop, SMA50 close exit, swing-low 20, no partial)
  looked like the only real lever; risk % scaled return and drawdown together; hold-out expectancy
  fell about 60%; the 6/8/10 ladder keeps S1 at 6–8 positions at a 28% win rate; NIFTY 500 regime
  rules never switched off in the 2018–20 midcap bear. Promotion criteria are fixed before any rerun
  (see "Promotion criteria").

- 2026-10-26: risk policy v2 in hat_live (owner: seed numbers too low for swing): risk 1%, 10 positions, open risk 10%, 3 per industry, ladder 6/8/10 at full size, health bands 12/18%, kill 20% (`/data/workspace/hat-data-isin/admin/policy-swing-100.json`). Candidate S1 research set `np`: v2 + vcp [2,6] + time stop off + SMA50 close exit + swing low 20 + no partial. Hold-out 2022–2026 run next.

- 2026-10-25: point-in-time NIFTY 500 from 2016; no backtest trades before 2016-01-01.
- 2026-10-25: S1 first. Other strategies stay but come after.
- 2026-10-25: independent S1 re-audit (`/data/workspace/audits/2026-10-25-s1-reaudit-fable.md`):
  no blockers. Features, RS, adjustments, membership, fills, exits, sizing and metrics checked
  by hand against raw bars. M1: the seed's `volume_pace` and the 5m `confirm: close` are not
  modelled by the daily-bar backtest. Decision: the research draft disables `volume_pace`
  (intraday variant) or uses `entry_timing: daily_close` + `volume_vs_avg: 1.5`; every intraday
  run notes that close-confirmation is not modelled (backtest fills on a tick through the pivot,
  so it is slightly optimistic vs live). Minors m1 (demerger placeholder memberships, no S1
  impact), m2 (no DP charge on sells), m3 (`avg50_volume` unset in the loop) go to open-items.
- 2026-10-25: funnel diagnosis (`/data/workspace/audits/2026-10-25-s1-funnel.md`) reproduced the
  baseline exactly (102 rows, 51 breaks, 20 add_to_loser): strictness, not a bug. VCP drops 99.7%
  of trend-template passers; the binding rule is "all of the last 6 legs tighten" (older deeper
  legs block BSE, CDSL, DEEPAKNTR, LAURUSLABS, TATAELXSI). Code fix in progress (builder
  hat/s1-pivot-reuse): no rows for held names, a pivot is used once. Next run after it merges:
  v2 + `criteria[vcp].params.contractions=[3,3]` (one change). Queued after: `close_vs_pivot`
  allowance for the pivot-confirmation lag, `max_high_spread_pct` (pivot mid-base, median 7.6%
  below the base high), and the exit set (MFE ~1R).
